Challenge-local artifact contract:

- Place harnesses, tests, expected output, and supporting files in this
  directory.
- Maintain a branch-local Success Criteria coverage table that names each
  published function or target plus its artifact path, current status,
  specification scope, and notes.
- PR descriptions should not separate "Verification entrypoints" from "Success
  Criteria Coverage". Instead, each function/target entry should carry its own
  harness path, start symbol, reproducer note, current status, and blocker
  note together.
- Distinguish verification harnesses from frontier reproducers or fail
  harnesses. Concrete-value reproducers do not count as verification.
- Keep changes organized so proof or semantic commits can be cherry-picked
  cleanly later.
- Record any exceptional dependency change in the generator and evaluator logs
  before landing it.

